/**
 * Decide how long to wait before the next attempt.
 * `attempt` is one-based and identifies the attempt that just failed:
 * returning a delay means another attempt will be made after that wait.
 * At most three attempts are made in total (including the first), so the
 * third attempt never yields a delay.
